"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":4866,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":103,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["ecmascript","eslint","javascript","linter","static-code-analysis"],"visibility":"public","forks":4866,"open_issues":103,"watchers":26698,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"It appears that when you use ES6 modules to `export` a function, the `no-unused-var` rule does not run properly on those function arguments. (vars declared in the function body still lint correctly)\n\n``` js\nfunction fn1({ a, b }) {\n  console.log(a);\n}\n\nfn1();\n\nexport function fn2({ x, y }) {\n  console.log(x);\n}\n\nfn2();\n```\n\nGiven the following config:\n\n``` js\n{\n  \"env\": {\n    \"es6\": true\n  },\n  \"ecmaFeatures\": {\n    \"modules\": true\n  },\n  \"rules\": {\n    \"no-unused-vars\": 2\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWhen I run this in the CLI:\n\n``` sh\n$ eslint --reset test.js\n\ntest.js\n  2:18  error  b is defined but never used  no-unused-vars\n\n✖ 1 problem (1 error, 0 warnings)\n```\n\nNotice that `fn1` gets linted correctly, but `fn2` does not report the unused `y` var.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/2678/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/2678/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":426930841,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDQyNjkzMDg0MQ==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/events/426930841","actor":{"login":"ilyavolodin","i